# Remu general rules

Always-on rules for the Remu repository. docs/RULES.md is the full rulebook and wins over this file. Written 2026-10-18.

## What Remu is

Remu is a "shop memory" for Indian retail: the hub recognises an opted-in returning member at the gate and the owner's phone shows a card so the owner can greet them by name. Three components: hub (`hub/`, Python 3.11), app (`app/`, Kotlin and Jetpack Compose, one Android app with Cashier mode and Owner mode), cloud (`cloud/`, Next.js 15, TypeScript, Supabase in Mumbai, Vercel bom1). Roles: member, owner, cashier. Member status: `pending_notice`, `active`, `withdrawn`, `expired`.

## Before coding

- Read docs/PRD.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/DESIGN.md, docs/RULES.md, TASKS.md and docs/MEMORY.md. For consent, members, templates, clips or webhooks also read docs/PRIVACY_AND_CONSENT.md and docs/SECURITY.md.
- Inspect the existing code before writing new code. Reuse the module that already does the job. Do not duplicate logic.
- Work one TASK id at a time, in TASKS.md order. Do not modify unrelated files. Do not widen scope past docs/PRD.md; the later-phase list stays out.
- For a change touching more than three files, or any schema, API, job or member status transition, write the plan (files, functions, tests, risks) before editing.
- Build prompts from docs/PROMPTS.md: CONTEXT, TASK, FILES, CONSTRAINTS, ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA, TESTING.
- When a document does not give a detail, choose the simplest option and write it down as an assumption. Anything that needs a human starts with "OPEN:".
- Finish every task with tests, lint, typecheck, `make check` at the root, a small conventional commit on a feature branch, a tick in TASKS.md and an update to docs/MEMORY.md (and an ADR in docs/DECISIONS.md for a decision).
- Keep the surprise: nothing at the gate reacts. No screen, sound, light or visible camera behaviour.

## Privacy invariants (code must never violate these)

1. No face photo is ever written to disk, database, log, crash report or cloud. Crops live in memory until embedded, then are dropped. The only footage is the 5-second match clip: encrypted on the hub, deleted after 30 days, LAN only, never uploaded.
2. Only the hub computes embeddings. The app sends an aligned crop with landmarks. Templates are scrambled with the per-shop key and never leave the hub.
3. The cloud never accepts or stores image bytes, templates or clips. Its request schemas have no field for them.
4. Members with status `pending_notice` are never matched. Only `active` templates are loaded into the matcher.
5. `consent_records` is append-only. Every row is written through the chain function. Withdrawal, deletion and expiry are new chained records, never edits or deletes.
6. "STOP" or "Remove member" deletes the template within one hour and logs `template_deleted_at` in the chain.
7. The nightly job deletes templates unseen for 1095 days and clips older than 30 days, and logs it.
8. An age estimate under 18 refuses enrolment. There is no override, flag or setting that bypasses it.
9. Unenrolled faces at the gate are discarded within seconds. Nothing is stored about non-members; a companion or passer-by may appear incidentally in a member's encrypted 5-second clip (LAN only, deleted after 30 days) and is never detected or indexed (docs/PRIVACY_AND_CONSENT.md section 12).
10. No PII in logs or error tracking: no names, phone numbers, notes, bill items, message text, crops or vectors. Log ids only.

These have no feature flag, no debug mode and no temporary bypass. If a task cannot be done without breaking one, stop and raise it.
